---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="Museum of Flight — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title"><a href="https://www.museumofflight.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Museum of Flight<Icon name="external" /></a> — Museum Apprentice Program</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Four-year apprenticeship &middot; 2016&ndash;2020</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        Over four years in the Museum Apprentice Program, I designed models and taught aerospace concepts
        to elementary school students. It was my first real exposure to a problem I still work on today
        in a very different form: <strong>taking something technically dense and finding the version of it that
        actually lands</strong> for someone with zero background.
      </p>
      <p class="blurb">
        The parallel to my current work is closer than it sounds — the same instinct that made me think
        about how to explain lift and thrust to an eight-year-old is the one I use now when I'm <strong>turning a
        data pipeline into a KPI an executive can act on</strong> without needing to understand the pipeline
        itself.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
